From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:08:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): exit-diag records carry a level; Slack list
 failures log one line; closed-ws keepalive no longer logs a loop error

- gateway-exit-diag.log: every record carries level (info for start/clean exit/SystemExit 0|75,
  error for crashes and non-zero exits). A supervised restart (exit 75) was graded an error by
  keyword-based log shippers on every hermes update. _make_exit_diag moves to
  hermes_cli/gateway_exit_diag.py.
- channel_directory: SlackApiError's two-line str() split one warning into two log records; the
  second ('The server responded with: {...invalid_auth}') was shipped as an error.
- tui_gateway.loop_noise: websockets' legacy keepalive awaits asyncio.shield(pong_waiter); on close
  the keepalive is cancelled and abort_pings fails the waiter, which asyncio logs as
  'ConnectionClosedOK exception in shielded future' at ERROR on every SSH-tunnel Desktop disconnect.
  Collapsed to a debug line, gated on the shield message + ConnectionClosed.

Burndown: hermes-gateway-mini
Fingerprints: 2cba464bd093 cc6bfc982678 6d8fbc34332b c1676bd05722 9433ad9fc697 08091931d56b
Fixes BB-59 BB-69 BB-76 BB-70 BB-71 BB-75

